# Outside el (§5.2), inside el++ (§5.4). Under el the axiom is ENUMERATED as
# omitted, so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent; under el++ it
# is decided: A is unsatisfiable.
#
# owl:bottomObjectProperty: el's CR1-CR7 have no built-in role semantics.
# Treated as an ordinary role, CR3 builds an edge for A ⊑ ∃bottomObjectProperty.⊤
# and A is reported SATISFIABLE: a missed unsatisfiability, i.e. a FALSE PASS.
# Hence out of el's profile, not ignored. el++ reads it as the empty role.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
                     owl:onProperty owl:bottomObjectProperty ;
                     owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ] .
